<dialog id="persistence-dialog">
  <form method="dialog">
    <header>
      <h3>Data Persistence</h3>
    </header>
    <div>
      <p>Your data is saved in the browser's storage. However, this data is not persisted forever due to browser restrictions unless the site asks for persistent storage.</p>
      <p>Therefore, the site is about to request permission to your browser to persist its data. Some browsers will give a pop-up asking you to approve this permission.</p>
      <p>Note that persistence is not required to use the site. Also, If you use the site regularly, data deletion is also unlikely to happen.</p>
      <p>Would you like for this site to request to persist its data?</p>
    </div>
    <footer>
      <button value="no" class="outline">No</button>
      <button value="yes">Yes</button>
    </footer>
  </form>
</dialog>
<dialog id="persistence-denied-dialog">
  <header>
    <h3>Data Persistence Denied</h3>
  </header>
  <div>
    <p>Your browser has denied data persistence permission.</p>
    <p>If this is intentional on your part, please refresh the page and select "No" on the dialog that appears</p>
    <p>Otherwise, refresh the page to try again.</p>
  </div>
  <footer>
    <button type="button" commandfor="persistence-denied-dialog" command="close" >OK</button>
  </footer>
</dialog>